  "full_response": "Software testing is a crucial part of the software development lifecycle, aimed at ensuring that the software meets its specifications and is free of defects. There are several main types of software testing, each serving different purposes and typically applied at different stages of development. Here are the primary types:\n\n1. **Unit Testing:**\n   - **Purpose:** To test individual components or units of the software to ensure each one functions correctly.\n   - **When Used:** During the development phase, immediately after a unit is implemented. It is typically done by developers.\n   - **Tools:** JUnit, NUnit, PyTest, etc.\n\n2. **Integration Testing:**\n   - **Purpose:** To test the interaction between different modules or components of the software.\n   - **When Used:** After unit testing, once various components are integrated together.\n   - **Types:** Top-down, bottom-up, and sandwich/hybrid approaches.\n   - **Tools:** TestNG, Postman for API testing, etc.\n\n3. **System Testing:**\n   - **Purpose:** To validate the complete and integrated software product to ensure it meets the specified requirements.\n   - **When Used:** After integration testing, as a whole.\n   - **Types:** Functional, performance, and security system testing.\n   - **Tools:** Selenium, JMeter, etc.\n\n4. **Acceptance Testing:**\n   - **Purpose:** To determine whether the software is ready for delivery by assessing it against business requirements.\n   - **When Used:** After system testing, and can be categorized into subtypes such as User Acceptance Testing (UAT), Alpha, and Beta testing.\n   - **Tools:** Cucumber, Tricentis Tosca, etc.\n\n5. **Functional Testing:**\n   - **Purpose:** To verify that the software functions as per the defined requirements.\n   - **When Used:** As part of system testing, focusing on user interfaces, APIs, databases, security, etc.\n   - **Types:** Black-box, white-box, and grey-box testing.\n   - **Tools:** Selenium, TestComplete, etc.\n\n6. **Non-Functional Testing:**\n   - **Purpose:** To assess the non-functional aspects such as performance, usability, reliability, etc.\n   - **When Used:** Throughout the testing process when performance (load, stress, endurance), usability, and security are a concern.\n   - **Types:** Performance testing, load testing, stress testing, security testing, usability testing, etc.\n   - **Tools:** JMeter, LoadRunner,",
